{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788352612,"nonce":"j3iaeBZnFnlBweqa9KRZEnLa0Ps=","message":"Correction to the comment above: the branch was rebased onto current `main` after it was written, so the commit ids there are dead. The branch is now 6 commits on top of `main`:\n\n```\n517d3c6  rwa: rotate the transcript at the segment cap instead of raising\n0e4fcc2  accept 4.2: --transcript takes a glob or a chain, not one directory\n13be3f8  rwa/selftest: cover the segment cap, rotation and the chain links\n1cedb4e  docs: the 999-step cap, segments and the chain (README + decisions log)\n11650bb  docs: a long run's transcript is a chain, in the two places a run reads\nb01156c  accept/4.2-play-loop.md: bring the selftest description up to what it runs\n```\n\nThe rebase was not cosmetic and it found a sixth thing to fix. The worktree\nwas cut at `c429dda`, and `accept/4.2-play-loop.py` had moved +426 lines on\n`main` since — `advance-discipline` (722c951) and `advance-wakes` (280fb78).\n**Both read the transcript, and `advance-discipline`'s casualty rule is an\nADJACENCY rule** — \"the very next command must not be another advance\" — so\nit breaks across a rotation exactly the way the wedge rule does. Its\n`transcript_steps` now takes the chain and flattens it segment-first, like\n`advance-invariants`. Had the branch been merged unrebased, the newer check\nwould have silently gone back to reading one directory.\n\nEverything green after the rebase, and the segment labels reach the newer\nchecks too:\n\n```\n$ bash rwa/selftest.sh\n  255 passed, 0 failed\n\n$ python3 accept/4.2-play-loop.py --selftest\nSELFTEST PASS\n\n$ python3 accept/4.2-play-loop.py RUNS/m1-20260901 --transcript 'transcripts/m1-20260901*'\nPASS  transcript-chain      5 segment(s): m1-20260901 -\u003e m1-20260901-s00 -\u003e …-s03\nFAIL  advance-discipline    m1-20260901/127-advance: ADVANCED BLIND — …\nWARN  advance-discipline    escape used — m1-20260901-s03/742-advance: through_casualties=…\n```\n\nAlso corrected while in the file: `accept/4.2-play-loop.md` described three\nmutations where the suite runs nine, and still carried \"**Status: the selftest\nhas NOT been run**\" from when it was authored on BORGES. It has been run, on\nthis box, green.","files":null}]}